From 2f3d7e2e5b56c3b6d7f8b7e8b155d159e194d786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bemly <bemly_@petalmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:14:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Sinytra patch 0006: SSL proceed via temporary cert overrides

android.webkit.SslErrorHandler.proceed() means 'continue despite the
invalid certificate'. GeckoView had no cert-override primitive and the
failed certificate is only reachable at error time, so:

- nsILoadURIDelegate.handleLoadError gains the failing channel (uuid
  bump; sole caller nsDocShell::DisplayLoadError). docShell.failedChannel
  was probed first and is unusable at delegate time: the JS-visible
  getter reads the error page document's failed channel, set only after
  this delegate call (nsDocShell.cpp GetFailedChannel -> doc->
  GetFailedChannel()).
- LoadURIDelegateChild captures securityInfo.serverCert DER (base64) on
  ERROR_CLASS_BAD_CERT and ships it with GeckoView:OnLoadError.
- LoadURIDelegateParent stashes it in the new global module
  GeckoViewCertOverride, whose ged event GeckoView:AllowCertError
  remembers a temporary nsICertOverrideService entry (Firefox
  Add-Exception semantics; consumed once, session-scoped).
- Provider side (Sinytra repo): SinytraSslErrorHandler in-package
  subclass routes the app's decision; proceed = allowError + reload.

Status: builds green, JVM locks green; device harness regression
pending (device disconnected). Temporary SINYTRA-0006 diagnostics in
the child actor are to be removed at finalization.
